!! HTML element fallback

When the symbol after a glyph marker matches a known HTML element name, the marker emits that element instead of the default. Vocab/Test is loaded via the type field: `text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Test`.

!!! Block (§ + element name)

§aside.b This becomes an `<aside>` because `aside` is a known block element

!!! Inline-pair (`{!em ...!}`)

This sentence has {!em emphasized text!} mid-stream, which becomes an `<em>` element.

!!! Default (no fallback when symbol is not an HTML name)

§whatever Just the default `<div>` from the SECTION marker, since `whatever` is not an HTML element.